Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:33:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 40/40] drama: backbone attention runs the reference's 64-key
 softmax tiles

Native kept a running max per key and per warp and merged the warps at the end. The reference extend kernel keeps one max per 64-key tile, with Triton's ex2.approx exp, div.full and fused multiply-adds. With the reference's tiles and arithmetic, the attention operator matches on 98.1% and 96.2% of its outputs at layers 3 and 39 (was 70.4% and 57.5%). The 182-token text fixture goes from relative L2 0.124 to 0.053, KL 0.024 to 0.0062, worst row 0.80 to 0.92. Tiles are fixed by key position, so chunk 1/7/128 and reset stay bit-exact.
